{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-unstable-atom-decay-channel","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel","kind":"proposition","title":"Unstable atom has a uniquely-determined decay channel","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-unstable-atom"],"tags":["decay","instability","ilp","phase-boundary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.decay_channel","text":"unstable-atom-decay-channel.md","leanSource":"unstable-atom-decay-channel.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Unstable atom has a uniquely-determined decay channel</em></p>\n<p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> be an atom-knot. If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> is <a href=\"#def:unstable-atom\">unstable</a> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, then its <strong>decay channel</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda^*(K, q)</code> is well-defined as the unique violated constraint.</em></p>\n"}
